From: Coding Dungeons maintainers
Subject: Bound Proxy ownKeys enumeration allocation before multiplication

Local defensive fix for https://github.com/bellard/quickjs/issues/535.
The array-like result can advertise a large length without allocating its
elements. On WASM32 the multiplication otherwise wraps to a small allocation.
Leave tab NULL on rejection so the existing failure cleanup is safe.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -48962,6 +48962,10 @@
     if (js_get_length32(ctx, &len, prop_array))
         goto fail;
     if (len > 0) {
+        if (len > SIZE_MAX / sizeof(tab[0])) {
+            JS_ThrowOutOfMemory(ctx);
+            goto fail;
+        }
         tab = js_mallocz(ctx, sizeof(tab[0]) * len);
         if (!tab)
             goto fail;
